.",[290,718,720],{"id":719},"idempotency-and-one-transaction","Idempotency and one transaction",[286,722,723,724,727,728,405],{},"Implement ",[303,725,726],{},"WebhookCalls.process(event, work)"," with these steps in ",[729,730,731],"strong",{},"one database\ntransaction shared by every wired driver",[733,734,735,743,746,753],"ol",{},[736,737,738,739,742],"li",{},"Serialize concurrent processing of the signed ",[303,740,741],{},"event.id",", using a unique key\nor lock. If that ID was already committed, return false without running work.",[736,744,745],{},"Retain the verified envelope, including unknown events, for audit and triage.",[736,747,748,749,752],{},"Await ",[303,750,751],{},"work()",": it applies built-in reactions, additional reactions, and dispatch.",[736,754,755],{},"Mark the ID processed and commit resource changes, bindings, audit, and outbox\nrecords together. Return true. Roll back everything if any step fails.",[286,757,758,759,762,763,765,766,769],{},"Do not commit a deduplication row before the work: a later failure would cause all\nretries to be discarded. Use the ",[729,760,761],{},"signed"," ",[303,764,741],{},", not the unsigned\n",[303,767,768],{},"Vatly-Event-Id"," correlation header. A timestamp check alone does not deduplicate.\nScope keys and rows by tenant\u002Fstorefront and mode.",[286,771,723,772,775],{},[303,773,774],{},"events.dispatch"," as durable outbox writes in that transaction. Send\nemail, provision external services, or make other network calls from a worker\nafter commit, not from inside a webhook reaction. Delivery order is not guaranteed;\nreconcile conflicting or out-of-order snapshots with the API.",[290,777,779],{"id":778},"what-fluent-persists","What Fluent persists",[781,782,783,796],"table",{},[784,785,786],"thead",{},[787,788,789,793],"tr",{},[790,791,792],"th",{},"Event",[790,794,795],{},"Built-in action when the repository is wired",[797,798,799,813,827,840,851,867,877,897,913],"tbody",{},[787,800,801,807],{},[8